# PHP & WordPress Standards

## Function naming

All theme functions use `hotw_*` prefix. Constants: `HOTW_THEME_VER`.

```php
// ✅ GOOD
function hotw_enqueue_assets() { ... }
add_action('wp_enqueue_scripts', 'hotw_enqueue_assets');

// ❌ BAD
function enqueue_assets() { ... }
```

## File organization

- Bootstrap and hooks: `functions.php`
- CPTs: `inc/post-type-{name}.php`
- Query/helpers: `inc/whats-on-*.php`
- Shared HTML shells: `page-template/`
- Sections: `template-parts/{area}/section-{name}.php`

## Template loading

```php
// Standard sections
get_template_part('template-parts/home/section', 'hero', $args);

// What's On only — shared parent variables
require get_template_directory() . '/template-parts/whats-on/section-calendar.php';
```

## Section $args pattern

```php
$defaults = array('title' => __('Default', 'heros-on-the-water'));
$args = isset($args) && is_array($args) ? wp_parse_args($args, $defaults) : $defaults;
```

## Security

- `ABSPATH` guard at top of every PHP file
- `esc_html()`, `esc_url()`, `esc_attr()` for output
- `wp_kses_post()` only for intentional HTML from ACF
- `do_shortcode()` for CF7 — document with phpcs ignore when needed

## Hooks

- Enqueue: `wp_enqueue_scripts`
- Theme setup: `after_setup_theme`
- CPT: `init` + `after_switch_theme` for rewrite flush
- ACF options: `acf/init`

## Filters (What's On)

- `hotw_whats_on_post_type` (default: `event`)
- `hotw_whats_on_event_date_meta_key` (default: `event_date`)
- `hotw_whats_on_upcoming_limit` (default: `-1`)
